# Line endings are pinned to LF everywhere.
#
# This is not housekeeping. The sibling research repository lost real time
# to test failures that turned out to be two line-ending conventions
# meeting in the same tree, and this harness is in the business of exact
# character accounting: the packer charges each admission its precise
# serialized cost against a hard ceiling, and the shadow trace asserts the
# reconstruction matches the library byte-for-byte. A CRLF checkout on one
# machine and an LF checkout on another is a silent way to make those
# comparisons disagree for reasons that have nothing to do with the
# mechanism.
#
# Windows developers: your editor should honour this. Git will hand you LF.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary-ish artifacts that must never be touched.
*.gguf   binary
*.sqlite binary
*.png    binary
*.ico    binary

# Generated; keep it out of diffs and language stats.
uv.lock            linguist-generated=true
ui/package-lock.json linguist-generated=true
